From: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] cix: remove pre-silicon EMU/FPGA dead code from vendor drivers

CIX vendor kernel patches carry dead code for internal development
platforms (emulators, FPGAs, evaluation boards) that will never run on
our shipping hardware (Sky1 ACPI-only production silicon). Remove it to
reduce complexity and maintenance burden, matching the equivalent
cleanup landed upstream in the (now-dormant) Sky1-Linux community tree
(github.com/Sky1-Linux/linux-sky1, commit
57e018a398248d7e5e4d798610df79a557c0629f,
"cix: remove pre-silicon EMU/FPGA dead code from vendor patches"),
re-derived here against our own post-series tree since our 170-patch
ACPI-glue/bug-fix series has independently touched several of the same
files and no longer matches that tree's vendor baseline byte-for-byte.

Changes, adapted hunk-by-hunk against our current tree:
- pci-sky1-cix.[ch] (vendor's pci-sky1.[ch], renamed by our own PCI
  driver split): remove PCIE_PLAT_FPGA/EMU enum values, the plat field,
  sky1_pcie_parse_plat(), the EMU early-returns in the reset/wake GPIO
  parsers, the conditional PHY power-on in sky1_pcie_reset(), and the
  "//DEBUG" FPGA early-return in sky1_pcie_probe(). Hardcode the
  production lane-enable masks (x2=0x4, x1_0=0x1, x1_1=0x2) in
  sky1_pcie_set_phy_pnn_rst_n() instead of branching on plat.
- phy-cix-pcie.c, phy-cix-usb3.c, phy-cix-usbdp.c: remove the
  #if CONFIG_ARCH_CIX_EMU_FPGA guards around the regmap read/write
  callbacks, keeping the bodies (they compiled out to empty stubs
  returning 0 on production silicon, which is not what we want).
- cdnsp-sky1.c: remove the #ifdef CONFIG_ARCH_CIX_FPGA APB timeout
  override block in cdnsp_sky1_drd_init().
- trilin_dptx.c/.h, trilin_drm.c: remove the CIX_PLATFORM_EMU/FPGA/
  INVALID defines and the platform_id field entirely. Always negotiate
  TPS4/TPS3/TPS2 by capability instead of gating on platform_id, always
  call trilin_dp_phy_ready(), always validate AUX reply byte counts,
  always run the enable_stream_clocks body (our own vid_clk2/vid_clk3
  MST work in dp_panel->source_id is unaffected -- the platform_id
  guard sat in front of it as a separate, removable precondition),
  always register the PHY in trilin_dp_register_phy(), and always read
  EDID via drm_get_edid() in trilin_dp_connector_get_modes() instead of
  faking a 4096x4096/640x480 EMU mode. The drm_dp_cec_set_edid() call
  present in the original upstream context is already absent from our
  tree (removed by earlier work) and is correctly not reintroduced
  here.
- armchina_aipu.h: fix "emum" -> "enum" typos in two kernel-doc
  comments (aipu_arch, aipu_isa_version). Trivial, no functional change.

arch/arm64/boot/dts/cix/sky1.dtsi is deliberately NOT touched: we boot
ACPI-only and carry no devicetree in this tree at all, so the upstream
patch's dtsi hunk (EMU/FPGA always-on timer property and GIC
redistributor-region #ifdef) has no applicable target here.

Every hunk in this patch was independently verified against the actual
post-170-patch-series tree (pristine v7.2-rc5 + patches-7.2/0001..0185
applied via git am, HEAD 9cbe7ca32927) rather than assumed from the
original vendor-baseline patch context, since several of these files
(trilin_dptx.c/.h, trilin_drm.c, pci-sky1.c/.h) have been independently
modified or renamed by our own 0154/0161/0169/0170/0176 (DPTX) and
0027/0029/0032/0059/0083/0099/0101/0102/0109 (PCI) series patches. No
conflicts were found: in every case the EMU/FPGA dead-code block was a
self-contained, still-untouched region that our own fixes happened to
sit next to rather than inside of.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
